Subject: [PATCH 09297/11362] File the red submission readiness gates found
 while closing the vLLM probe gap

Six tests in the exp4744/exp4754 readiness-gate family fail, and a HEAD-baseline
comparison over the same selection confirms all six were already red before the
vLLM probe work -- these are standing defects, not regressions from it.

They matter more than an ordinary red test because these modules ARE the check that
SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG describes the run the kernel launches. While they fail for
every configuration, correct or not, they cannot distinguish one from the other, so
the project has no working mechanical readiness answer before a slot is spent.

Partial cause: the gates compare against the live generator constants, and the
fixtures still named gemma-4-31B-it after the move to Qwen3.8-27B. Fixing the exp4754
fixture did not clear it, so at least one further cause is unfound. Filed rather than
chased, because half-correcting a gate family is how one ships looking green.

